            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "updated patch with just a tweak to checkindex.\n\nnow no apis actually require that the codecs norms impl implements getArray. maybe someone wants a more compact/sparse datastructure for some reason (LUCENE-830)... if they want this, thats fine.\n\nBut all our similarities use getArray. I think thats a fair tradeoff... if you want to use some crazy datastructure, fine but you must use a custom sim, too.",
